= Sequence alignment — Technical =

For pairwise alignment, dynamic programming optimizes a score over substitutions and gaps. A simple global recurrence is <pre>F(i,j)=max{F(i-1,j-1)+s(x_i,y_j), F(i-1,j)-g, F(i,j-1)-g}</pre>with boundary conditions. Local alignment modifies the recurrence to allow restart at zero. Probabilistic/HMM approaches represent related assumptions differently.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* alignment ≠ proof of homology
* sequence similarity ≠ homology by definition
* highest score ≠ biologically correct alignment under every model

